  "items": [
    {
      "name": "Headbonk",
      "type": "weapon",
      "img": "icons/skills/melee/shield-block-bash-blue.webp",
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "value": "<p>The Goomba's only attack is running into enemies headfirst, using its disproportionately hard cranium as a bludgeoning weapon. The headbonk is not sophisticated. It is not elegant. It is a small creature running at you with its head down and hoping that the impact accomplishes something useful. Against unarmored, distracted, or very unlucky targets, it occasionally does.</p><p>The headbonk's primary tactical value is distraction rather than damage. A Goomba headbonking an enemy forces that enemy to spend an action dealing with the Goomba rather than engaging more valuable targets. If the enemy stomps the Goomba (which typically requires one attack and deals any amount of damage, since Goombas have 7 hit points and AC 8), the Goomba has accomplished its mission: one enemy action consumed, one moment of tactical advantage created for the unit behind it.</p><p>Goombas who survive headbonk attempts are surprised and mildly confused by the experience. Success is not what training prepares them for.</p>",
          "chat": "<p>It runs at you head-first with the total commitment of someone who has accepted that this is probably the end and has decided to make it count.</p>"
        },
        "unidentified": {
          "name": "Headbutt",
          "description": "<p>A small creature charging headfirst with more determination than tactical viability.</p>"
        },
