    {
      "name": "Stomp Vulnerability",
      "type": "feat",
      "img": "icons/skills/melee/hand-grip-hammer-spiked-blue.webp",
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "value": "<p>Goombas are critically vulnerable to attacks from above. Any attack that strikes a Goomba from a higher elevation—jumping attacks, falling objects, dropped items, gravity—deals double damage. This vulnerability is biological: the Goomba's cranium is hard for headbonking purposes but the body beneath is soft and compresses easily under downward force. A single stomp from a creature of Medium size or larger is typically sufficient to defeat a Goomba regardless of the attacker's strength score.</p><p>This vulnerability is so well-known that it defines the Goomba's tactical identity. They operate on flat terrain whenever possible. They avoid positions beneath ledges, balconies, or elevated platforms. They cluster together so that stomping one requires landing among the others, creating at least marginal retaliatory opportunity. And they maintain a permanent upward awareness that gives them advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks to notice threats from above, a survival instinct honed by millennia of being the thing that gets stepped on.</p>",
          "chat": "<p>Don't stomp on them. They know you want to stomp on them. They've arranged their entire tactical doctrine around the assumption that you will try to stomp on them. Stomp on them anyway because it works every time.</p>"
        },
