    {
      "name": "Strength in Numbers",
      "type": "feat",
      "img": "icons/skills/social/diplomacy-peace-alliance.webp",
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "value": "<p>Goombas are individually negligible threats. In groups, they become something approaching dangerous through sheer volume—not because individual capability increases but because the number of actions required to eliminate them creates opportunities for more capable allies to capitalize on. When three or more Goombas are within 5 feet of each other and attacking the same target, each Goomba gains advantage on its headbonk attack roll as the collective assault from multiple directions makes effective defense more difficult.</p><p>This ability has saved Goomba lives exactly never, but it has delayed enemy advances, consumed enemy resources, and created the momentary distractions that Koopa Troopa squads behind them need to set up effective defensive positions. The Goombas don't know this. They think they're fighting. What they're actually doing is buying time with their bodies, and the Troop's tactical doctrine has been built around this function for so long that nobody questions whether it's ethical.</p>",
          "chat": "<p>One Goomba is a speedbump. Three Goombas are a slightly taller speedbump. Ten Goombas are a genuine tactical consideration, which is the most a Goomba can aspire to.</p>"
        },
