    {
      "name": "Resigned Determination",
      "type": "feat",
      "img": "icons/magic/life/heart-glowing-red.webp",
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "value": "<p>Goombas are immune to the frightened condition. Not because they're brave—bravery implies a choice between fear and action, and Goombas don't experience that choice. They simply walk forward. They have always walked forward. Walking forward into danger is what Goombas do, the way breathing is what lungs do, the way falling is what dropped objects do. It is not courage. It is nature. And nature doesn't require saving throws.</p><p>This immunity makes Goombas unexpectedly useful against enemies who rely on fear effects. Dragon frightful presence, undead horrifying visage, banshee wailing—none of it stops a Goomba. The Goomba continues walking forward with its expression of mild annoyance, headbonking whatever terrifying entity it encounters with the same determination it would apply to a locked door or an unfamiliar obstacle. The Goomba doesn't understand why the dragon is surprised. The Goomba doesn't understand most things. The Goomba walks forward.</p>",
          "chat": "<p>It's not brave. It's not fearless. It simply doesn't have the cognitive architecture for fear to interrupt its walking-forward subroutine. The dragon is confused. The Goomba is not.</p>"
        },
